ks a conditional or automatic result."},{"start":34,"end":39,"surface":"何と難しい","grammar":"なんと＋形容詞","meaning_en":"なんと plus an adjective forms an exclamation."},{"start":41,"end":45,"surface":"こぼすと","grammar":"Vると","meaning_en":"A plain-form predicate followed by と marks a temporal or conditional clause."},{"start":49,"end":61,"surface":"自然そのものを写せという","grammar":"引用＋という","meaning_en":"A quoted imperative followed by という introduces reported wording and modifies a following noun."},{"start":81,"end":84,"surface":"これは","grammar":"Nは","meaning_en":"は marks これ as the topic."},{"start":84,"end":91,"surface":"作り話だったが","grammar":"Nだったが","meaning_en":"The past copula followed by が links a contrastive clause."},{"start":95,"end":99,"surface":"無邪気に","grammar":"ナ形容詞＋に","meaning_en":"に converts an adjectival noun into an adverbial modifier."},{"start":125,"end":129,"surface":"塗ったが","grammar":"V-たが","meaning_en":"A past-form predicate followed by が introduces contrast or concession."},{"start":132,"end":140,"surface":"灰色に黄が混じり","grammar":"Nに混じる","meaning_en":"に marks the substance that another substance mixes into; the り-form connects onward."},{"start":140,"end":145,"surface":"漆のような","grammar":"Nのような","meaning_en":"のような forms an attributive comparison or simile."},{"start":145,"end":153,"surface":"斑がある本来の姿","grammar":"連体修飾節","meaning_en":"A plain-form clause before a noun functions as a relative modifier."},{"start":152,"end":162,"surface":"姿とは似ても似つかず","grammar":"Nとは＋固定否定表現","meaning_en":"とは marks the comparison target before the fixed expression meaning not resemble at all."},{"start":163,"end":171,"surface":"説明しようのない","grammar":"V-ようのない","meaning_en":"This construction expresses that there is no way or possibility to perform the verb."},{"start":174,"end":179,"surface":"目さえない","grammar":"Nさえ＋ない","meaning_en":"さえ emphasizes an extreme item within a negative construction."},{"start":187,"end":194,"surface":"熱心さに免じて","grammar":"Nに免じて","meaning_en":"に免じて means making an allowance out of consideration for the noun."},{"start":203,"end":208,"surface":"耐えられず","grammar":"V-られず","meaning_en":"Potential られる combined with literary negative ず means without being able to perform the verb."},{"start":220,"end":228,"surface":"用を足しに行こう","grammar":"Vます語幹＋に行く","meaning_en":"The stem plus に行く marks purpose; the final verb is in volitional form."},{"start":225,"end":232,"surface":"行こうとすると","grammar":"Vようとすると","meaning_en":"ようとする marks an attempt or intention, and とすると marks when or as that occurs."},{"start":242,"end":247,"surface":"怒鳴られた","grammar":"V-られる＋た","meaning_en":"The passive auxiliary followed by た marks a past passive event."}]}